course: dictionary
lesson: 10227
title: Tobacco: plant, product and risk
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tobacco is a plant. Its leaves are dried and then smoked in cigarettes, cigars and pipes, or chewed. The dried leaves themselves are also called tobacco.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «Cigarettes contain tobacco and nicotine» means the dried leaves in a product. «Sugar, cotton and tobacco back to Europe» means crops that were grown on farms and traded.
explain: Tobacco is harmful to health. It contains nicotine, which is addictive, and smoking causes lung disease, heart disease and cancer. That is why it is illegal to sell it to children.
fact: Tobacco is a plant whose dried leaves are smoked or chewed.
fact: The word «tobacco» can also mean the dried leaves prepared for smoking.
fact: Nicotine in tobacco is addictive, which means it is very hard to stop using once you start.
fact: Smoking causes lung disease, heart disease and cancer.
fact: In history, tobacco was grown on big farms called plantations and traded between countries.
exercise: «Cigarettes contain tobacco and nicotine.» What is tobacco here? | A type of weather | A big ship | A kind of sweet | *A plant whose dried leaves are smoked or chewed
exercise: «Smoking causes lung disease, heart disease and cancer.» What does this tell you about tobacco? | It is good for your lungs | It makes you taller | It is only used for cooking | *It is harmful to health
exercise: Copy the one word that names a crop grown on plantations: «In the triangle of trade, ships took goods from Europe to Africa, and sugar, cotton and tobacco back to Europe.» | Europe | *tobacco | ships | triangle
test: «It is banned inside workplaces and pubs, so smokers go outside even in the rain.» Why do smokers go outside? | Outside is warmer | *Smoking is banned inside, so they must go outside | They like the rain | The pubs are closed
test: Which part of tobacco is addictive? | Sugar | Metal | Cotton | *Nicotine
exam: In «Ships took sugar, cotton and tobacco back to Europe», what is tobacco? | A town in Africa | A ship | A kind of cloth | *A crop grown on farms and traded
